WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:05.560
- How do you know if a business
idea is worth pursuing?

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.170
So my take on that is

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:11.390
if you think about what
you are going to uniquely

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:12.470
bring to the table.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:14.540
Sometimes I've been at a
restaurant with a friend

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:16.437
and they're like, "Oh, this
restaurant's doing so well.

00:00:16.437 --> 00:00:17.950
"I think I could do this,"

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.550
and they start thinking about maybe I'll

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.270
open up another restaurant just like that

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:22.103
across the street.

00:00:22.103 --> 00:00:25.350
Well, I think my friends in that situation

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:28.360
are probably underestimating how much work

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.470
that the restaurant
we're in had put into it,

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:32.673
how much thought they put into it.

00:00:32.673 --> 00:00:33.980
And also if you open up
an identical restaurant

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.020
across the street, well
that's just going to hurt

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:37.650
both of your businesses and neither of you

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.710
might have a viable business.

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:41.810
Another thing is you
could look at a business

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:43.260
that someone else
started and you might see

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.800
the cash register running and
there's a lot of customers,

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:48.580
but you don't realize
everything, all of the costs,

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:50.630
all of the risks that that person took on.

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:52.600
Their rent might be a lot.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:54.350
You might just be going
through during the busy time,

00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:55.790
and if you go the next day during lunch,

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:58.041
there might not be anyone there.

00:00:58.041 --> 00:01:00.100
And so, it's very easy
to always see things

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.860
that the grass is greener
on the other side.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:03.240
Most entrepreneurs will tell you

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:07.280
that even the most successful ventures

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.960
went through their dark periods

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:10.380
and went through a period

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:13.170
where it looked like it was going to fail.

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:16.095
It didn't look like it
was going to work out.

00:01:16.095 --> 00:01:19.690
And so what I would say if
you have a business idea,

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:21.920
is one, think about what you're going to

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:23.060
uniquely bring to the table.

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:26.390
Maybe it is an idea that no
one's ever thought about before.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:28.460
But maybe it is an idea that people

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:29.320
have thought about before,

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:31.770
but you have a unique
way of approaching it,

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:34.560
or you have unique
skills, or a unique team

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:35.540
that can approach it right,

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:39.480
or you kind of see the nexus
of several of these things.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:43.423
And I would try to test the
idea as well as possible.

00:01:44.922 --> 00:01:46.880
Can you put out some
advertising for your business

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:50.660
before it even exists and
see if people respond?

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:52.850
Can you build a prototype of a product

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:55.320
and see if people want it?

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.620
And the more that you
can test it in that way

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:00.387
and say, "Wow, there's actually
a product market fit here,

00:02:00.387 --> 00:02:01.677
"or a service market fit here;

00:02:01.677 --> 00:02:05.790
"people really want what this idea is,"

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:07.990
then I think you might be on to something.

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:10.060
Obviously the ideal is you
even start the business

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:13.630
on a small scale without
necessarily going all in yet

00:02:13.630 --> 00:02:17.210
and seeing that wow, there's
a lot of demand for this.

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:21.100
So once again, no right
answer here always.

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.450
When you're starting a business,

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:24.360
you really just have to
prepare yourself mentally

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:26.910
that there will be rough patches.

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.190
But if you can come up with something

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:31.880
and have a unique take on it and test it,

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:35.000
and it's actually getting
traction with folks,

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.050
and you're able to get the capital,

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.900
and you yourself have the
capital you've saved up, maybe,

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:43.943
if things get a little bit rough
as you start your business,

00:02:43.943 --> 00:02:46.543
I think you might be in a
good position to start it.

